}
,"name": "Simple Macaroni and Cheese"
,"aggregateRating": {
"@type": "AggregateRating",
"ratingValue": "4.6",
"ratingCount": "1151"
}
,"cookTime": "PT15M"
,"keywords": "publisher-tested"
,"nutrition": {
"@type": "NutritionInformation"
,"calories": "630 kcal"
,"carbohydrateContent": "55 g"
,"cholesterolContent": "100 mg"
,"fiberContent": "2 g"
,"proteinContent": "27 g"
,"saturatedFatContent": "21 g"
,"sodiumContent": "777 mg"
,"sugarContent": "8 g"
,"fatContent": "34 g"
,"unsaturatedFatContent": "0 g"
}
,"prepTime": "PT10M"
, "recipeCategory": ["Dinner"]
,"recipeCuisine": ["American"]
,"recipeIngredient": [
"1 (8 ounce) box elbow macaroni",
"0.25 cup butter",
"0.25 cup all-purpose flour",
"0.5 teaspoon salt",
"ground black pepper to taste",
"2 cups milk",
"2 cups shredded Cheddar cheese" ]
,"recipeInstructions": [
{
"@type": "HowToStep"
,"image": [
{
"@type": "ImageObject",
"url": "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/KzZUo7phRa4Bsra_1V2yFvoUrlA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/23869-simple-macaroni-and-cheese-ddmfs-step01-a59c7635633c47aaa545963b5401b02a.jpg"
}
]
,"text": "Gather the ingredients."
} ,{
"@type": "HowToStep"
,"image": [
{
"@type": "ImageObject",
"url": "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/jBC5Y1qwmSX1Pz7eEqxwHUu44So=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/238691-Simple-Macaroni-And-Cheese-mf-Step1_001-f3f1e3416cf742778ac39c1db3d0ebea.jpg"
}
]
,"text": "Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Cook elbow macaroni in the boiling water, stirring occasionally until tender yet firm to the bite, about 8 minutes."
} ,{
"@type": "HowToStep"
,"image": [
{
"@type": "ImageObject",
"url": "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/rxq90SJQtzOaEl0jAvtytOaZZww=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/238691-Simple-Macaroni-And-Cheese-mf-Step2_002-cff2a9558167448180ac13d7aadb0f64.jpg"
}
]
,"text": "Meanwhile, melt butter in a saucepan over medium heat."
} ,{
"@type": "HowToStep"
,"image": [
{
"@type": "ImageObject",
"url": "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/BXgdxNwF17gAp6CQb67qMPcY8hQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/238691-Simple-Macaroni-And-Cheese-mf-Step3_003-a053939c742147199b60130b0e22f750.jpg"
}
]
,"text": "Whisk in flour, salt, and black pepper until smooth, about 5 minutes."
} ,{
"@type": "HowToStep"
,"image": [
{
"@type": "ImageObject",
"url": "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/YOhN5cl0H-SjTO-BQWRn_WKpBTk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/238691-Simple-Macaroni-And-Cheese-mf-Step4_004-c60819e1ab6946e89c884ab3fc573536.jpg"
}
]
,"text": "Slowly pour in milk, while constantly stirring; cook and stir until mixture is smooth and bubbling, about 5 minutes, making sure the milk doesn’t burn."
} ,{
"@type": "HowToStep"
,"image": [
{
"@type": "ImageObject",
"url": "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/F0ePI61vokw9PNDuGVWmgGiDkss=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/238691-Simple-Macaroni-And-Cheese-mf-Step5_006-7019c891342041a997f31f04d246e799.jpg"
}
]
,"text": "Add Cheddar cheese and stir until melted, 2 to 4 minutes."
} ,{
"@type": "HowToStep"
,"image": [
{
"@type": "ImageObject",
"url": "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/DiRuRRjLwbBLV_VF29TRPZcrC1g=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/238691-Simple-Macaroni-And-Cheese-mfs-Step6_007-ea19705a4daa4e1ba37359cda9a70ab6.jpg"
}
]
,"text": "Drain macaroni and fold into cheese sauce until coated."
} ,{
"@type": "HowToStep"
,"image": [
{
"@type": "ImageObject",
"url": "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/xI5g0WBP8yPHwRt1Nt5WudTctzE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/238691-Simple-Macaroni-And-Cheese-mfs_008-b32db5aa505041acbe958aedb81d29e9.jpg"
}
]
,"text": "Serve hot and enjoy!"
} ]
,"recipeYield": "4"
,"totalTime": "PT25M"
,"review": [
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Nikolai"
}
,
"reviewBody": "Made it almost exactly like the recipe stated, super easy on the first try. All I added was a dash of paprika and a little extra salt. One note, the amount of milk you add will heavily depend on where you live, altitude, and humidity. I live in a dry, high altitude location so even though I halved the recipe, I used over a cup of milk to get the right consistency. The people that complain of a thin sauce either live at very low altitude or their roue wasn't cooked enough when they started adding the milk and cheese. Also, grainy mac and cheese is the result of adding the cheese too quickly. To ensure a smooth texture, add it slowly and melt completely before adding more, which the recipe didn't explain. If it's too thick, add more milk, and if you think it tastes like flour, you didn't cook the flour and butter for long enough, leaving it mostly raw. To remedy that you can carefully cook it for longer or start over."
},
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "ToughPecan1386"
},
"reviewBody": "Followed all the directions on how to make it. Things I changed were - doubled the noodles, added 1/8 tsp dried chili, 2 tsp dry mustard, 3 chopped garlic cloves, ¼ cup chopped jalapeños. (I like spice :)) also doubled the cheddar, saved one cup for on top, then added panko and a bit of Parmesan and baked it for 30 minutes at 350. Yum!",
"datePublished": "2023-11-21T01:17:12.296Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "BriefRoe2495"
},
"reviewBody": "This is my go-to macaroni and cheese recipe. I like to put it in a casserole dish, top with some grated Parmesan, and put it in the oven at 350 for 30 mins. It comes out perfect every time.",
"datePublished": "2023-06-20T17:55:36.313Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "QuickWhisk4053"
},
"reviewBody": "KEEPER! My frugal gourmet tips - which I discovered by accident while short on ingredients (my partner made everyone at work try it, calling this my 'marry me macaroni'): 1. I caramelised x3 white onions first, then made the white sauce on top of them. Takes ages, but if you have time, makes this incredible. 2. Use garlic flavoured avocado oil (with butter) for these onions! Bought it by mistake and the flavour in the end is unbelievable. 3. Add smoked bacon and broccoli. I oven baked it! 4. Cheapskate emergency topping: crumbled two slices of bread into the pan I fried the bacon in (and previously the onions) + crumbled garlic flavoured crackers + butter and then poured on mac and cheese with some grated cheese before going in the oven. 5. I was able to get away with just cheap cheddar cheese and no parmesan etc because of the garlic avo oil!",
"datePublished": "2025-02-02T18:49:39.718Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "2"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Angelina"
},
"reviewBody": "Indeed, this is a 'very basic' Mac &amp; Cheese recipe, which (IMO) needs some improvement. As written, you could of had something similar by cooking up a box of Kraft. The next time I made it, I added in a couple of tsps. of yellow mustard. Also, instead of using the pre-packaged (orange) Cheddar, I grated in (REAL) white Cheddar cheese (Cabot's), and also a good handful of grated Gruyere cheese. I use evaporated milk in casseroles, since it makes for a creamier consistency, and I used the next larger size elbows. I topped the Mac &amp; Cheese w/whole grain Panko breadcrumbs. I hate to criticize, but this version was a whole lot better than the original recipe.",
"datePublished": "2018-02-03T17:00:51.890Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "RV Living"
},
"reviewBody": "As fast as promised. I used Organic No Salt Seasoning + 1/2 tsp salt and it was great. Also had medium shells on hand instead of elbows. Cooked the shells for 4 mins @ high pressure in the Instant Pot while making the white/cheese sauce. This is a great recipe and I will make it often. Not much muss or fuss and hit the comfort food spot. YUM!",
"datePublished": "2024-10-17T02:05:57.181Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Michelle Soter"
},
"reviewBody": "I followed the recipe, but added some onion and mustard powder to the rue, and langostinos when mixing the pasta and sauce. I then poured everything in a pan, covered with breadcrumbs and baked at 350 degrees for a few minutes until bubbling. I then turned the oven on to broil for just a minute to brown the top. It was magnificent!",
"datePublished": "2025-02-02T23:52:53.721Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Krystal Wave"
},
"reviewBody": "Omg this was so easy and tasty! I just threw out my old Mac and cheese recipe! \n\nI did add 1/2 cup more cheese and substituted 1 cup whipping cream for 1 cup milk and added garlic powder. Topped with buttered bread crumbs (crushed in zip lock) and under the broiler for 30 sec. \n\nAMAZING!",
"datePublished": "2017-11-30T01:47:10.200Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Tinkerbella"
},
"reviewBody": "Very good for being so simple. No buying special cheeses or anything, I had everything on hand. I used 2 cups of macaroni and 3 cups freshly shredded cheddar and there was plenty of sauce. I also added 2 cans of tuna and a package of peas and we just had it for dinner. Macaroni cheese tuna fish and peas is a favorite lazy dinner, lol.",
"datePublished": "2017-02-02T03:55:43.737Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "tiffanytiffanym"
},
"reviewBody": "I added garlic powder, onion powder, salt, pepper and a bit of truffle oil!!! I used sharp cheddar, mild cheddar and a fiesta blend. This was a great base recipe that you can easily customize with different additions.",
"datePublished": "2019-07-12T19:45:10.503Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "NimbleCorn2692"
},
"reviewBody": "I like to add 1cup of Prego Artisan Four cheese sauce to the cheese sauce. Also, save 1/4 cup of the pasta water when draining the pasta. Addi ng the saved water back to the pasta makes the cheese sauce stick to the pasta better. Enjoy",
"datePublished": "2024-01-28T17:36:32.553Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Z"
},
"reviewBody": "I was having some doubts since I only had aldi brand shredded cheese, but this came out great. Just added a little extra salt and garlic powder and mustard powder. Adding the milk and cheese slowly was a great tip!",
"datePublished": "2026-09-24T13:21:22.309Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Chris Locke"
},
"reviewBody": "Excellent recipe, very simple and adapts well to changes. I had about four different types of cheeses sitting in the fridge that had to be used up, so they all went in, and with great success. Very creamy and tasty.",
"datePublished": "2026-09-09T03:05:38.648Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Tara L"
},
"reviewBody": "Much better served when just made, will try to halve the recipe next time. I love leftovers but mac and cheese does stick together and requires additional liquid to reheat.",
"datePublished": "2026-08-31T01:42:49.843Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Catherine"
},
"reviewBody": "Definitely a keeper.",
"datePublished": "2026-08-29T15:46:25.985Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Jennifer"
},
"reviewBody": "I have made several of the viral Mac n cheeses recipes that turn out just ok. This was made in 15 min and it was the right consistency and it tastes great! I’m so happy I found this recipe!!!",
"datePublished": "2026-08-13T01:59:40.012Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "4"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "milo"
},
"reviewBody": "too starchy",
"datePublished": "2026-07-18T16:56:23.690Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Greta Backatcha"
},
"reviewBody": "I have celiac's so when i make mac and cheese I'm always trying different recipes because the consistency isn't just right with GF flour. Finally this recipe has the perfect ratios! Adding onion powder was a great tip.",
"datePublished": "2026-06-27T01:53:09.858Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Kimluvs2kook"
},
"reviewBody": "I love Stouffers Mac and cheese but this is even better!! I did bake it with cheddar cheese and parmesan cheese on top for 30 minutes after it was done, absolutely delicious!!!",
"datePublished": "2026-06-21T00:42:13.239Z"
}
,
{
"@type": "Review",
"reviewRating": {
"@type": "Rating",
"ratingValue": "5"
},
"author": {
"@type": "Person",
"name": "Brook"
},
"reviewBody": "So fast and easy! I added red chili flakes and some garlic for more flavor and sometimes bread crumbs",
"datePublished": "2026-06-15T22:31:07.880Z"
}
